// Under `pin uid = principal.id`, a pin to an attribute, which is not symmetric, a Login response
// logs `uid: "someone"`. Both ingest it: the field need only be logged. It does not match alice's
// `Read`, whose `principal.id` is "alice", so the `Read` is denied; after a login that logs `uid:
// "alice"` it is allowed.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::response{}
};
